Make room for every digit of a large integral number in awk.
fmt_num() converts an integral number to a string with "%.0f" into the
240-byte g_buf, but an integral double can have 309 digits, so numbers
of about 1e239 or more lost their last digits: "x = 1e300; print
length(x "")" printed 239 instead of 301. Enlarge the buffer to hold
the largest double with its sign.

---
 editors/awk.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/editors/awk.c
+++ b/editors/awk.c
@@ -92,7 +92,8 @@
 	OPT_W = 1 << OPTBIT_W
 };
 
-#define	MAXVARFMT       240
+/* Room for "%.0f" of any double: up to 309 digits and a sign */
+#define	MAXVARFMT       320
 
 /* variable flags */
 #define	VF_NUMBER       0x0001	/* 1 = primary type is number */
